<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 25 October, from 1147 to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1147">1147 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">879 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Afonso I of Portugal takes Lisbon after a four-month siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With crusader help, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-kongo">Afonso I</a>, the first king of Portugal, ended a siege begun on 1 July and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> from the Moors. The siege, seen as pivotal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, was one of the few Christian victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso I of Portugal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1400">1400 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">626 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Geoffrey Chaucer dies in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-chaucer">Geoffrey Chaucer</a> died, according to the date on his tomb in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> Tales, written in English rather than French or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, helped establish English as a literary language.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1415">1415 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">611 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry V defeats a larger French army at Agincourt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry V's outnumbered and exhausted army, largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a>, defeated the French at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a> as heavily armoured knights struggled across muddy ground. Many French nobles were killed or captured.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1760">1760 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">266 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George III becomes king of Great Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George II died suddenly at Kensington Palace, and his 22-year-old grandson succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a>. His 60-year reign saw the loss of the American colonies and victory over Napoleonic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1854">1854 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">172 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Light Brigade charges at Balaclava</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A misunderstood order sent British light cavalry charging down a valley ringed by Russian guns. About 270 of some 670 riders were killed or wounded, and Tennyson's poem made the charge a byword for courage and blunder.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">Brigade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zagonyi's Union cavalry wins the First Battle of Springfield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Springfield, Missouri, Major Charles Zagonyi, commander of the bodyguard of General Frémont, won a minor Union victory over Missouri State Guard recruits through a charge widely covered by the media. Federal troops occupied the city two days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union troops defeat Sterling Price's Confederates at Marais des Cygnes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After their defeat at Westport on 23 October, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pound-sterling">Sterling</a> Price's Confederate raiders withdrew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a>; Union troops then defeated them at Marais des Cygnes in Linn County, at Mine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> and at the Marmiton River.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan launches its first organised kamikaze attacks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leyte">Battle of Leyte</a> Gulf, Japanese pilots deliberately crashed their aircraft into American ships, sinking the escort carrier St. Lo. Suicide attacks became a central Japanese tactic for the rest of the war.</p></div></li></ol>
